1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,796
This video shows what happens when a record has nowhere to go,

2
00:00:05,796 --> 00:00:09,070
and how to find the record that holds things up.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:16,110
It uses the route from video 1: tutorial-in, through tutorial-in-parse, to tutorial-out.

4
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:19,796
Say tutorial-out should get only clean records.

5
00:00:19,796 --> 00:00:21,557
Open the route.

6
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:28,550
Add a condition on the line to tutorial-out: smeltr.exception equals null.

7
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,589
Save it on a branch, tutorial-clean-only.

8
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,924
Open it for review, and deploy it.

9
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:55,874
Now send a record that isn't JSON, and a clean one after it.

10
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,381
Back in smeltr, Status shows an issue.

11
00:00:59,381 --> 00:01:00,796
Open Issues.

12
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,446
tutorial-in is blocked.

13
00:01:04,446 --> 00:01:10,790
No condition took a record, and Unmatched is answered with block.

14
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:13,090
smeltr hasn't accepted the record.

15
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,518
Kafka isn't told it was read, and a sender that pushes is told to try again later.

16
00:01:18,518 --> 00:01:21,893
So nothing is lost, as long as the source keeps it.

17
00:01:21,893 --> 00:01:27,188
The clean record waits too, since it's behind the bad one in the same partition.

18
00:01:27,188 --> 00:01:30,150
Workers reading other partitions carry on.

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,975
To see the record, open the Map, and select tutorial-in.

20
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:40,308
Capture shows the record holding it up.

21
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,893
Here it is: checkout, card expired.

22
00:01:45,893 --> 00:01:47,350
No condition took it.

23
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,490
It failed to parse, so it's tagged.

24
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:56,710
Your new condition sends only untagged records, so nothing takes it.

25
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:01,098
Stop, and save it as a sample, so you can test a fix with it.

26
00:02:01,098 --> 00:02:04,899
It goes on a new branch, tutorial-exceptions.

27
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:11,399
Check on learning.

28
00:02:11,599 --> 00:02:13,778
No destination takes a record.

29
00:02:13,778 --> 00:02:16,121
What happens by default?

30
00:02:20,521 --> 00:02:24,667
It's Unmatched, and the source blocks until the config changes.

31
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:29,215
smeltr doesn't accept the record, so it waits at the source.

32
00:02:30,115 --> 00:02:33,457
Where do you see the record that holds a source up?

33
00:02:37,857 --> 00:02:41,228
Select the source on the Map, and capture it.

34
00:02:42,128 --> 00:02:47,299
Next, you give these records a place to go, and the source flows again.
